olating or unable to come to the lecture room for any reason, we will publish a zoom link in advance.","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"pIO0nV3x60"}],"key":"B9NEIk4x2J"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summary of Course Assessment","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"r97O2jPKKe"}],"identifier":"summary-of-course-assessment","label":"Summary of Course Assessment","html_id":"summary-of-course-assessment","implicit":true,"key":"Xdd542oDJb"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"There will be 5 short quizzes during the semester that will help you to calibrate your knowledge from the course material for each module and which you can use for revision. The first of these quizzes will be a refresher on plate tectonics which you will be allowed to re-take after an optional tutorial. (20% on these quizzes)","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"qbTEy07H0K"}],"key":"QMxC5b8Czj"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lab-based assessments will be worth 20% of the course in total. One assessment will be an exercise on interpreting sandbox models that you will be running in the lab. The second will be a mapping exercise.","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"BbwWgWUlUa"}],"key":"hBQwVzf0K5"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"There will be a poster- or slide-based- presentation  and final report that together make up 20% of the course assessment.","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"AwA6D7l